// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! ramlib.library's functions: the module loader's one call of its own
//! (SINCE 1.4). What it does otherwise it does by standing in front of
//! exec's OpenLibrary and OpenDevice. The base is the one exec keeps with
//! SetRamLib; the call is exec's, made when a module goes.
##basetype RamLibBase
##name ramlib.library
##bias 4
##public
/// The segments a library or device was loaded in, unloaded once it has
/// gone: what its Expunge handed back to exec at its last close or in the
/// low-memory flush. Segments ramlib did not load are left alone; null
/// does nothing. Called by exec, after the Expunge returned; it does not
/// wait, and runs inside AllocMem's low-memory handler too.
void UnLoadModule(?*anyopaque seg_list)
##end
